From a3034a67df4e26e903a0cd073b6c8cdce4574aa4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Azathothas <ajamx101@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 07:30:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] GitHub #725: pod applies PODNET_POLICY to each flow
 (netns, seccomp, --serve)

podnet-netns has a hook of the egress policy: rules::set_permit. Each
decision of the pod (select_chain, select_chain_udp) asks it before the
rules of -r. src/main.rs sets it to podnet::policy::permit after it
installs the policy. A refused flow gets the answer of a reject rule:
ECONNREFUSED or EACCES (netns: a reset or a drop), SOCKS5 0x02 and
HTTP 403 (class Policy) at the door. The line names the reason of the
policy ("refused by PODNET_POLICY: the rule ..."); the flow log names
the rule "policy". --learn does not send such a flow through -x.

Tests: tests/pod_policy.rs (each backend and the door), and
rules::tests::the_policy_refuses_before_the_rules.
